Q6 CONCLUSION & MIGRATION STRATEGY:
1. Use PRAGMA user_version for migration tracking at app startup.
2. Prefer ADDITIVE evolution (ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN): works seamlessly without tripping triggers.
3. Historical records remain immutable: old records get NULL/defaults, maintaining audit veracity.
4. For breaking structural changes, use atomic transaction migration: drop triggers -> rename -> create new -> copy -> recreate triggers -> commit.
5. Use Views (e.g. v_legacy_action_records) if legacy code requires old column representations.
